// The named diagnostic for an explicit `[&name]` capture the pre-pass cannot
// type.  `u` comes out of a tuple destructuring, which neither compiler infers
// before typecheck, so the by-ref list is a claim about a name that is not
// there — and saying so beats letting the name fall through to `undefined
// variable` from inside the substituted body.
//
// Lives in the tc-errors corpus: the program is REJECTED, and the contract is
// the first line — message and position — byte-exact with the reference.

fn run<F: |int|->int>(f: F, x: int) -> int { f(x) }

fn main() {
    let t = (1, 2);
    let (u, w) = t;
    let g = [&u] |x: int| -> int x + u;
    println(run(g, 5));
    return;
}
